Error [jet.PerfNameNotLiteral]: The name given to `perf.zone` is not a string literal.
  --> E3406_perf_zone_name_not_literal.jet:4:22
    |
  4 |     _zone: perf.zone(name)
    |                      ^^^^
 Why: A zone's or plot's name is its site's: the program passes the literal's text as it is, so naming a site allocates nothing and every row of the site carries the same name on the `jet perf view` timeline.
 Fix: Write the name as a string literal, such as `perf.zone("physics")`; to tell cases apart, give each its own site and name.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E3406
